Biome's CLI for WASI preview1 (wasm32-wasip1-threads). The commands that
run in-process work (check, format and lint are certified); what needs
sockets or a child process does not.

- service/wasi.rs: WASI has no domain sockets and cannot start a daemon, so
  `--use-server` finds no server and start/lsp-proxy/__run_server/
  __print_socket report ErrorKind::Unsupported. __run_server refuses before
  it starts the file watcher (the runtime would wait for it forever).
- --watch on check/format/lint: WASI has no file system events; refuse
  with the same Unsupported diagnostic instead of hanging.
- `biome upgrade` replaces the binary with an HTTPS download; on WASI it
  explains that the package manager upgrades it, and self_update/ureq
  (rustls, ring) are left out of the wasi dependency graph.
- main: wasi-libc starts every program in "/" (std::env::current_dir()
  is "/" on slicc-kernel, while relative paths reach the process's
  working directory through the kernel's `.` preopen), and Biome resolves
  paths and configuration from current_dir. On WASI main changes into the
  real working directory: PWD when it names the same directory as `.`
  (device and inode, as POSIX shells check PWD), otherwise the path
  getcwd(3)'s walk finds (`..` up to the root, each directory looked up
  in its parent). A parent can set a child's directory without rewriting
  PWD (Node's child_process.spawn with `cwd`); taking that stale PWD made
  Biome resolve relative paths against the parent's directory ("No files
  were processed in the specified paths"). Without the chdir, `extends`
  in biome.json does not resolve packages from the project's
  node_modules. libc, a unix dependency already, is a wasi one too, for
  stat(2).
- biome_fs: std::env::temp_dir() panics on WASI ("not supported by WASI
  yet") and ensure_cache_dir() falls back to it, since there is no
  platform cache directory; on WASI it takes TMPDIR, or /tmp.

Built with RUSTFLAGS=--cfg tokio_unstable (tokio refuses io-std, net and
rt-multi-thread on wasm without it). Other platforms are unchanged.

Upstream: not filed (Lars decides).

